# IT Support Incident Case Studies

This document records practical troubleshooting scenarios completed as part of the Enterprise IT Support & Service Operations Lab.

The incidents were tracked using ServiceNow and investigated using the Windows enterprise lab consisting of DC01, SRV01 and CLIENT01.

---

## Incident 1 — User Unable to Sign In

### User Report

Alex Taylor reported that he was unable to sign in to his corporate account.

### Initial Checks

The investigation focused on the user's Active Directory account rather than immediately resetting the password.

Checks included:

- Account enabled/disabled status
- Account lockout status
- User identity
- Domain account configuration

### Root Cause

The Active Directory account was locked out.

### Resolution

The account was unlocked through Active Directory Users and Computers.

### Verification

The account status was checked again after the change to confirm that the lockout had been cleared.

### Key Learning

A login failure does not automatically mean that the password needs resetting.

A useful troubleshooting sequence is:

`Account exists → Enabled? → Locked? → Password status → Correct domain/account`

